# reco-now's own vocabulary — an EXTENSION of packs/gst/ontology.ttl, not a
# parallel copy. Corrected per plans/119-architecture-audit.md §3.1/§6.
#
# No classes here: reco-now's rows mint `gst:PurchaseInvoice`/
# `gst:Gstr2bInvoice` directly (see graphowl_client.py), because that
# distinction is already exactly what packs/gst's ontology draws — "Purchase
# invoice (taxpayer's register)" is reco-now's "books" dataset, "GSTR-2B
# invoice (as filed by the supplier)" is its "gstr2b" dataset. Minting
# reco:BooksInvoice/PortalInvoice as separate classes (the first version of
# this file did) would have been the same duplication mistake one layer up.
#
# Six properties: exactly the fields in ext-apps/Reco/backend/app/main.py's
# FIELD_LABELS that packs/gst/ontology.ttl does not carry. Every other field
# reuses a gst: predicate directly — see graphowl_client.py's PREDICATES
# table for the full 17-field mapping, split by which namespace owns each.

@prefix reco: <https://reconow.dev/pack#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

reco:hsnCode              rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "HSN Code" .
reco:imsStatus            rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "IMS Status" .
reco:noteType             rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Note Type" .
reco:voucherType          rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Voucher Type" .
reco:voucherNumber        rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Voucher No" .

# A note references the invoice it corrects, by number, as the source data
# carries it. Not modelled as a graph edge: the referenced invoice may not
# be in the same upload, and a dangling `reco:Ref` would be a broken edge
# rather than a missing fact.
reco:originalInvoiceNumber rdf:type reco:Property ; reco:label "Original Invoice No" .
